    "Description": "Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7 is a platform for Java applications based on the WildFly application runtime. This release of Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.4.26 serves as a replacement for Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.4.25, and includes bug fixes and enhancements. See the Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.4.26 Release Notes for information about the most significant bug fixes and enhancements included in this release.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* jackson-databind: jackson-databind: Ignored properties can be unexpectedly modified (CVE-2026-54515)\n\n* jgroups: artemis cluster password leak via jgroups spoof (CVE-2026-49364)\n\n* openjdk-orb: Incomplete fix for CVE-2026-15560,unauthed class loading via IIOP in EAP (CVE-2026-84725)\n\n* artemis-server: Apache Artemis — session hijack via missing authentication (CVE-2026-57967)\n\n* artemis-server: artemis core protocol permits unauthed queue creation (CVE-2026-49362)\n\n* cxf: Apache CXF: Remote Code Execution via unsafe deserialization of JMS ObjectMessage (CVE-2026-66909)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS\nscore, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s)\nlisted in the References section.",
